WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.517
HR supplies most of the
person, but not everything,

2
00:00:03.517 --> 00:00:07.238
and every gap needs a named
writer or it becomes drift.

3
00:00:07.238 --> 00:00:12.465
Contractors aren't in the HR system, so
each of their facts gets its own authority,

4
00:00:12.465 --> 00:00:15.237
like the contract record
or the PIV system.

5
00:00:15.237 --> 00:00:19.813
Device attributes come from device
provisioning, never from the user's record.

6
00:00:19.813 --> 00:00:24.424
And where someone signs in from is
a sign-in signal, not an HR fact.

7
00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:28.142
On the right is the design
that survives the HR cutover:

8
00:00:28.142 --> 00:00:33.263
an agency-owned key, standard data
elements, and one door into the directory.

9
00:00:33.263 --> 00:00:36.620
That makes the switch a source
swap rather than a redesign.
